  "hindi": "जैसे दो निचोड़ने के पत्थर, वैसे तुम दोनों उसी प्रयोजन के लिए ध्वनि करते हो; जैसे दो गिद्ध निधि वाले वृक्ष की ओर। जैसे दो ब्रह्मा यज्ञ में उक्थ का पाठ करने वाले, जैसे दो दूत, बुलाने योग्य, जनों के, बहुत स्थानों में।",
  "english": "Like two pressing stones you sound to that very purpose; like two vultures toward the tree that has a store. Like two Brahman priests in the rite, reciting hymns; like two messengers, to be invoked, belonging to the people, in many places.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The two addressees are not named in the verse (the Aśvins are named in verses 7 and 8, not applied here). 'tat id artham jarethe' is tentative: jarethe 'you two sound' (√jṝ), artham 'purpose, aim'. nidhimantam 'having a store' (nidhi 'store, treasure'; whether a nest or treasure is meant is not stated). janyā 'belonging to the people' tentative; 'havyā janyā' could be taken as qualifying the Aśvins directly.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.039.1a",
   "002.039.1b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
   "ग्रावा॑णेव॒ तदिदर्थं॑ जरेथे॒ गृध्रे॑व वृ॒क्षं नि॑धि॒मन्त॒मच्छ॑",
   "ब्र॒ह्माणे॑व वि॒दथ॑ उक्थ॒शासा॑ दू॒तेव॒ हव्या॒ जन्या॑ पुरु॒त्रा"
  ],
