  "hindi": "जैसे दो सींग, हमारे लिए सबसे आगे इस ओर आओ; जैसे दो खुर, वेगों से काँपते हुए। जैसे दो चक्रवाक, प्रातःकाल के प्रति, हे उज्ज्वल दोनों, इस ओर मुड़कर आओ, जैसे दो रथ-चालक, हे शक्तिशाली दोनों।",
  "english": "Like two horns, foremost, come hither to us; like two hooves, quivering with speed. Like two cakravāka birds at dawn, bright ones, turned hither, come like two charioteers, O mighty ones.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The comparisons are literal and the point of each simile is not interpreted. prati vastoḥ 'at dawn' tentative (each dawn); usrā read as 'bright ones' (usra), may also be 'cows'. jarbhurāṇā 'quivering, darting' tentative. cakravāka: a bird name, kept untranslated.",
